cal policy implications.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u5.840\"}]},{\"alignment\":\"DIFFERENT_OR_UNENCODED_QUESTION\",\"assumptions\":[\"The supplied classifications and factual stipulations are true.\",\"No later amendment or other applicable authority displaces the selected clause.\"],\"candidate_id\":\"node.ea4d19630f8cab09065b1909\",\"case_id\":\"25ec66.pending.application\",\"facts\":[],\"rationale\":\"The case asks whether the existing approval or authorisation process continues for a pending application. The candidate concerns eligibility for new approval relief and treats a legacy pending application as an exclusion; it does not encode the separate process-continuation proposition or its negation.\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809\"}]},{\"alignment\":\"DIFFERENT_OR_UNENCODED_QUESTION\",\"assumptions\":[\"The supplied classifications and factual stipulations are true.\",\"No later amendment or other applicable authority displaces the selected clause.\"],\"candidate_id\":\"node.ea4d19630f8cab09065b1909\",\"case_id\":\"25ec66.uk.ucits\",\"facts\":[],\"rationale\":\"The case asks whether a UK-authorised UK UCITS scheme is included in the circular's definition of UCITS funds. The candidate's Boolean predicate assumes scope but does not encode the definitional inclusion question itself or its negation.\",\"source_evidence\":[{\"quote\":\"For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.\",\"unit_id\":\"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556\"}]}],\"unresolved\":[]}"}}
